MAJOR_VERSION=5
STANDARD_VERSION=3
RELEASE_VERSION=0
PRERELEASE=1
DEV_VERSION=8
DESCRIPTION=AI tooling: reuse before you implement, plus the DevOps team skill. AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md gain a Reuse before you implement section (research existing drivers, helpers and contracts in depth before writing new code, never two functions that do the same thing, extend instead of copying, add one shared helper and point every caller at it), mirrored for Cursor in .cursor/rules/reuse_before_implement.mdc. The devops-multi-agent-team skill from Homework Central is imported under .cursor/skills, .cursor/agents and .cursor/commands (goal, code-review, repro, triage, create-subagent), adapted to this repo: its Researcher writes a reuse map before a Coder starts, its Reviewers block duplicated new code, its CodeQL policy covers C and C++, and this repo's versioning and driver-boundary rules take precedence. .cursor/thoughts is git-ignored except its keepfile. First use (issue 384, D1): one shared hex codec, kernel/include/fl/hex.h (fl_hex_nibble, fl_hex_encode, fl_hex_decode, header-only), replaces the copies in user_db.c, bridge.c, kq_delivery.c and password_hash.cpp with identical output (checked against the old build with a fixed-salt password hash); new make test_hex. Rules: one .ver per PR, added with the first real push after QA and Security approval and only edited afterwards; the DevOps skill staffs 2 to 3 subagents per function and moves idle seats to busy ones. Not covered: Buildkite, Linear, Sonar, Snyk, Composio and Mainframe are named by the skill but optional here, and no CodeQL workflow exists in this repo yet. Items 2 and 3 (D2, D3): fl_fs_read_file in server_shared_fs.c (one open, fstat, regular files only, size cap, no truncated read, wipe on failure) replaces read_all, the letter-store reader and the lab reader, and header-only fl_fs_basename in kernel/include/fl/path.h replaces the strrchr copies in kq_checkpoint.c, lab_kq.c, net_file_delivery.c, fs_provider.c and fat32_host_files.c; new make test_fs_helpers. Differences: a directory, FIFO or device now gives a generic error, a file that changes during the read fails instead of truncating, the lab reader is capped at FL_KQ_LETTER_MAX, and a NULL path gives an error or an empty name instead of a crash. QA now ends with a bug hunt instead of CodeQL, and Coders send questions to standing Review, Security and QA seats. The wasm lab build was not compiled here (no emcc). Other hex copies remain in server_shared_digest.c, net_wifi_db.c, disk.c, cluster.c, commands.c and lab_kq.c.
